  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "A solid box is \\(15\\) cm by \\(10\\) cm by \\(8\\) cm. A new solid is formed by removing a cube \\(3\\) cm on a side from each corner of this box. What percent of the original volume is removed?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(4.5\\)",
    "B": "\\(9\\)",
    "C": "\\(12\\)",
    "D": "\\(18\\)",
    "E": "\\(24\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "A rectangular box has \\(8\\) corners, so \\(8\\) cubes are removed. These cubes do not overlap: together, cuts from opposite ends extend only \\(3+3=6\\) cm along a dimension, less than even the box's shortest dimension, \\(8\\) cm.\n\nThe original box has volume\n\\[\n15\\cdot10\\cdot8=1200\\text{ cm}^3.\n\\]\nEach removed cube has volume \\(3\\cdot3\\cdot3=27\\text{ cm}^3\\), so the total removed volume is \\(8\\cdot27=216\\text{ cm}^3\\). The percentage removed is therefore\n\\[\n\\frac{216}{1200}\\cdot100\\%=18\\%.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{18\\%}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
